271
00:27:32,004 --> 00:27:33,255
For a promotion?

272
00:27:33,256 --> 00:27:34,382
Performance reviews?

273
00:27:35,258 --> 00:27:36,801
I simply felt bad for you.

274
00:27:37,677 --> 00:27:39,512
I didn't do a single thing wrong

275
00:27:39,762 --> 00:27:41,764
but I let it go because
I felt bad about the situation.

276
00:27:43,057 --> 00:27:44,350
And this is how you behave?

277
00:27:49,188 --> 00:27:51,899
I am just as uncomfortable

278
00:27:53,025 --> 00:27:54,110
as you are.

279
00:27:55,278 --> 00:27:57,029
You aren't the only one suffering.

280
00:27:57,488 --> 00:27:58,531
So stop making a fuss.

281
00:28:00,157 --> 00:28:01,951
I'm done treating you like a senior.

282
00:28:02,451 --> 00:28:04,077
You brought this upon yourself

283
00:28:04,078 --> 00:28:05,371
and you'll bear the consequences.

284
00:28:07,039 --> 00:28:08,040
Understood?

285
00:28:13,713 --> 00:28:14,714
Get back to work.

286
00:28:30,688 --> 00:28:33,649
This happened on my first morning off
as team leader.

287
00:28:35,609 --> 00:28:37,153
Both of you,
pull yourselves together.

288
00:28:37,695 --> 00:28:39,029
Don't get caught up in this nonsense

289
00:28:39,030 --> 00:28:41,364
when you should be focusing
on your work.

290
00:28:41,365 --> 00:28:42,575
You're not kids anymore.

291
00:28:43,784 --> 00:28:46,077
- Yes, sir.
- I'm sorry.

292
00:28:46,078 --> 00:28:47,121
I'm sorry.

293
00:29:07,308 --> 00:29:08,309
Come in.

294
00:29:15,232 --> 00:29:17,151
This is the sales record
for last week.

295
00:29:18,611 --> 00:29:20,446
And here's the report
on the new project.

296
00:29:21,030 --> 00:29:23,865
At this rate, I'll be buried
under all this paperwork.

297
00:29:23,866 --> 00:29:27,828
And I graphed the shifts
in consumer patterns year-over-year.

298
00:29:28,704 --> 00:29:29,954
Here are the overseas brand sales

299
00:29:29,955 --> 00:29:32,833
categorized by region,
as you requested.

300
00:29:33,209 --> 00:29:34,794
Do you know what your problem is?

301
00:29:35,795 --> 00:29:38,046
I have so many.
I'm not sure which one.

302
00:29:38,047 --> 00:29:39,924
You don't give me
a moment to breathe.

303
00:29:40,341 --> 00:29:42,009
You need to pace my workload.

304
00:29:43,844 --> 00:29:45,678
That, I didn't consider.

305
00:29:45,679 --> 00:29:47,807
The same goes
for how you treat your subordinates.

306
00:29:48,849 --> 00:29:49,934
I heard Team 5 is a mess.

307
00:29:50,601 --> 00:29:51,684
Yes.

308
00:29:51,685 --> 00:29:53,144
Mr. Gong surprised me.

309
00:29:53,145 --> 00:29:54,604
He's got quite a temper.

310
00:29:54,605 --> 00:29:55,856
He learned that all from you.

311
00:29:56,440 --> 00:29:57,817
And I learned it from you, Ms. Park.

312
00:29:58,984 --> 00:30:00,986
How's Laknes looking?
Do you think it'll go well?

313
00:30:01,404 --> 00:30:03,029
You know Mr. Gong.

314
00:30:03,030 --> 00:30:04,364
He always delivers
above expectations.

315
00:30:04,365 --> 00:30:06,075
He's got a good grasp
of the big picture too.

316
00:30:07,993 --> 00:30:11,122
Big-picture thinking is
what causes the biggest disasters.

317
00:30:11,497 --> 00:30:13,581
- Keep an eye on him.
- Yes, ma'am.

318
00:30:13,582 --> 00:30:15,708
And help him smooth things over
with Mr. Yang.

319
00:30:15,709 --> 00:30:17,586
What is bound to happen will happen.

320
00:30:17,920 --> 00:30:19,922
But you can't leave a mess
sitting there.

321
00:30:21,048 --> 00:30:22,049
Understood, ma'am.

322
00:30:22,341 --> 00:30:23,342
If you'll excuse me.

323
00:30:29,974 --> 00:30:33,727
I told you pacing is key, Mr. Jang.

324
00:30:45,072 --> 00:30:47,116
- Ju-hui.
- Yes, Ms. Joo?

325
00:30:47,366 --> 00:30:48,491
Are you looking for something?

326
00:30:48,492 --> 00:30:50,411
I'm looking for last year's catalog.

327
00:30:50,661 --> 00:30:52,078
For what?

328
00:30:52,079 --> 00:30:55,457
Osiris's design for this year
seems familiar.

329
00:30:55,458 --> 00:30:56,917
I want to dig around and check.

330
00:31:00,087 --> 00:31:02,590
Let me ask you something.

331
00:31:03,257 --> 00:31:06,635
Is your team taking over any brands
from another team?

332
00:31:07,720 --> 00:31:08,888
Like what?

333
00:31:09,138 --> 00:31:10,347
I'm just wondering

334
00:31:10,931 --> 00:31:14,935
if you are supposed to get anything
from Team 4 or 5.

335
00:31:18,397 --> 00:31:21,025
I'm not sure about such details.

336
00:31:22,735 --> 00:31:23,777
You aren't?

337
00:31:24,069 --> 00:31:26,029
Do you want me to look into it?

338
00:31:26,030 --> 00:31:27,656
No, it's fine.

339
00:31:28,782 --> 00:31:32,703
Let me know
if you hear anything, okay?

340
00:31:33,579 --> 00:31:34,580
Sure, Ms. Joo.

341
00:31:35,915 --> 00:31:37,583
- Keep up the good work.
- Thanks.

342
00:32:04,610 --> 00:32:06,237
Hello, Mr. Jang.

343
00:32:08,447 --> 00:32:09,448
I'm sorry?

344
00:32:16,914 --> 00:32:17,957
I knew it.

345
00:32:18,457 --> 00:32:20,125
I knew I'd find you here.

346
00:32:23,629 --> 00:32:25,797
Everyone probably knows I'm up here.

347
00:32:25,798 --> 00:32:27,591
That's why nobody else is coming up.

348
00:32:28,092 --> 00:32:29,425
I'm allowed up here, right?

349
00:32:29,426 --> 00:32:31,387
After all, I was your first mentor.

350
00:32:32,555 --> 00:32:34,765
I really started off
on the wrong foot.

351
00:32:36,976 --> 00:32:39,352
Man, the guy who got smacked
is working hard

352
00:32:39,353 --> 00:32:41,730
but the guy who threw the punch
is in distress.

353
00:32:42,356 --> 00:32:43,774
Where did that even come from?

354
00:32:45,067 --> 00:32:47,361
It was bound to happen
sooner or later.

355
00:32:47,611 --> 00:32:49,947
Once? You should've done it
dozens of times already.

356
00:32:52,491 --> 00:32:53,992
So should I pat myself on the back?

357
00:32:53,993 --> 00:32:54,994
No.

358
00:32:55,536 --> 00:32:58,496
You should've either done it
dozens of times

359
00:32:58,497 --> 00:32:59,999
or kept swallowing it until the end.

360
00:33:01,792 --> 00:33:04,253
It must be driving you nuts
to go back down there and face him.

361
00:33:05,713 --> 00:33:06,714
Mr. Jeong.

362
00:33:07,423 --> 00:33:09,008
Remember back when we were
on Mr. Jang's team?

363
00:33:09,425 --> 00:33:11,676
I used to get chewed out
all the time.

364
00:33:11,677 --> 00:33:12,720
I know.

365
00:33:13,095 --> 00:33:14,513
I'm only saying this now

366
00:33:14,972 --> 00:33:17,140
but we used to bet
on when you'd quit.

367
00:33:17,141 --> 00:33:19,059
The most ridiculous thing
back then was...

368
00:33:20,060 --> 00:33:21,144
Wait, you placed bets?

369
00:33:21,145 --> 00:33:22,228
Yes.

370
00:33:22,229 --> 00:33:23,314
Go on. Tell me.

371
00:33:24,523 --> 00:33:26,775
Anyway, the most ridiculous thing was

372
00:33:27,234 --> 00:33:29,736
when Mr. Jang completely
tore me apart

373
00:33:29,737 --> 00:33:32,697
and then acted all friendly,
throwing an arm around my shoulder.

374
00:33:32,698 --> 00:33:34,657
Tell me about it.
I fell for that many times.

375
00:33:34,658 --> 00:33:37,827
So I was 100 percent convinced
he was a psycho, a sociopath

376
00:33:37,828 --> 00:33:39,537
or whatever kind of path out there.

377
00:33:39,538 --> 00:33:41,831
I still think so.
That guy's a walking mental case.

378
00:33:41,832 --> 00:33:44,918
But now that I'm in those shoes

379
00:33:46,086 --> 00:33:48,255
I wonder if I should go down there

380
00:33:49,256 --> 00:33:50,674
and act all friendly with him.

381
00:33:51,634 --> 00:33:54,553
Whenever Mr. Jang pulled that stunt

382
00:33:54,928 --> 00:33:57,388
I took it as a sign to sweep it
under the rug and move on.

383
00:33:57,389 --> 00:33:58,598
Why?

384
00:33:58,599 --> 00:34:00,183
Because corporate life is what it is.

385
00:34:00,184 --> 00:34:01,644
You just sweep it under the rug.

386
00:34:02,645 --> 00:34:04,188
Yang Jun-ho will probably
do the same.

387
00:34:04,772 --> 00:34:07,274
Should I do the same as Mr. Jang?

388
00:34:07,900 --> 00:34:10,151
Then you'll turn
into a psychopath as well.

389
00:34:10,152 --> 00:34:11,487
- Oh, jeez!
- Oh, my gosh!

390
00:34:11,987 --> 00:34:12,988
Oh, man.

391
00:34:13,697 --> 00:34:15,698
How long have you been standing here?

392
00:34:15,699 --> 00:34:19,119
Look at you punks,
badmouthing your boss at work.

393
00:34:21,038 --> 00:34:22,706
You, follow me.
We're going somewhere.

394
00:34:24,750 --> 00:34:25,917
As for you, we'll talk tomorrow.

395
00:34:25,918 --> 00:34:27,461
Sir, that's not what I meant.

396
00:34:28,295 --> 00:34:29,630
Hey, cover for me.

397
00:34:30,631 --> 00:34:32,675
You called him a psychopath first.

398
00:34:55,280 --> 00:34:59,076
If you put half as much heart into me
as you do beef

399
00:34:59,410 --> 00:35:00,828
I'd carry you on my back.

400
00:35:03,372 --> 00:35:05,082
This is your treat today.

401
00:35:05,749 --> 00:35:08,043
It's the unwritten rule to buy beef

402
00:35:08,544 --> 00:35:10,545
if you get caught
badmouthing your boss.

403
00:35:10,546 --> 00:35:12,506
I was planning
on treating you, anyway.

404
00:35:13,298 --> 00:35:14,299
Look at this punk.

405
00:35:14,675 --> 00:35:17,343
No excuses, no denial...

406
00:35:17,344 --> 00:35:18,886
How shameless of you.

407
00:35:18,887 --> 00:35:20,180
Thank you.

408
00:35:23,142 --> 00:35:24,226
Anyway...

409
00:35:25,018 --> 00:35:27,896
Are you sorting out the brands
to hand over to Team 1?

410
00:35:28,939 --> 00:35:30,107
Wait.

411
00:35:30,649 --> 00:35:32,276
Is that officially locked in
for Team 1?

412
00:35:32,526 --> 00:35:34,445
Why bother asking?
You know how this works.

413
00:35:35,404 --> 00:35:37,030
Let's get Kim his promotion.

414
00:35:38,657 --> 00:35:41,200
I'll sort everything out
and hand it over by this week.

415
00:35:41,201 --> 00:35:42,535
What's there to think about?

416
00:35:42,536 --> 00:35:44,455
Just dump over
all the borderline ones.

417
00:35:44,913 --> 00:35:46,832
They might look borderline to others

418
00:35:48,167 --> 00:35:50,209
but they're like my own kids.

419
00:35:50,210 --> 00:35:51,919
That's why I gave you Laknes.

420
00:35:51,920 --> 00:35:54,923
A kid who'd get into SNU
without going to cram school.

421
00:35:56,133 --> 00:35:57,718
You punk.

422
00:36:02,931 --> 00:36:05,893
This may be overstepping

423
00:36:06,560 --> 00:36:09,980
but is Mr. Jeong completely
written off for promotion?

424
00:36:12,483 --> 00:36:13,900
He's the one refusing to do it.

425
00:36:13,901 --> 00:36:15,319
It's not like I'm blocking him.

426
00:36:28,123 --> 00:36:29,666
Hey, over here.

427
00:36:31,084 --> 00:36:32,085
I told him to come.

428
00:36:32,920 --> 00:36:34,378
It's not like you're sworn enemies.

429
00:36:34,379 --> 00:36:35,714
He can be here.

430
00:36:37,841 --> 00:36:38,967
But...

431
00:36:39,802 --> 00:36:40,927
Are you leaving?

432
00:36:40,928 --> 00:36:42,970
I'll take care of the bill.

433
00:36:42,971 --> 00:36:44,139
You guys finish up.

434
00:36:44,765 --> 00:36:45,766
Oh, right.

435
00:36:46,141 --> 00:36:47,392
When I acted friendly with Mr. Jeong

436
00:36:47,768 --> 00:36:51,230
I didn't mean to sweep
all the grudges under the rug.

437
00:36:51,814 --> 00:36:53,398
I meant to clear the air and move on.

438
00:36:55,651 --> 00:36:57,820
What are you waiting for?
Go sit down.

439
00:36:58,654 --> 00:36:59,655
I'm sorry?

440
00:37:15,128 --> 00:37:17,714
I was really craving beef today.

441
00:37:19,049 --> 00:37:22,135
But I ended up
having it with you, Mr. Yang.

442
00:37:23,512 --> 00:37:25,722
Why the sudden switch back
to formality?

443
00:37:26,515 --> 00:37:28,767
Obviously, I'll keep
speaking formally to you.

444
00:37:31,395 --> 00:37:33,146
Why are we pushing things this far?

445
00:37:36,567 --> 00:37:38,651
I think we need a drink for this.

446
00:37:38,652 --> 00:37:39,653
Yes, absolutely.

447
00:37:46,743 --> 00:37:47,744
Mr. Yang.

448
00:37:48,912 --> 00:37:50,330
Can I ask you something?

449
00:37:51,331 --> 00:37:52,583
Go ahead and shoot.

450
00:37:54,459 --> 00:37:58,297
Am I such an important person
in your life?

451
00:38:01,633 --> 00:38:04,303
I'm not sure what you mean by that.

452
00:38:05,596 --> 00:38:06,680
You see

453
00:38:07,723 --> 00:38:10,434
a major personal event
happened to me last weekend.

454
00:38:11,310 --> 00:38:12,811
It was life-changing enough...

455
00:38:15,772 --> 00:38:17,608
to make me reflect on my whole life.

456
00:38:19,735 --> 00:38:21,486
But thinking about it all weekend...

457
00:38:23,530 --> 00:38:26,408
I realized my biggest obstacle
in life right now...

458
00:38:29,369 --> 00:38:30,579
is none other than you.

459
00:38:35,626 --> 00:38:36,752
So I asked myself

460
00:38:37,210 --> 00:38:40,546
if you were really
that important a person to me.

461
00:38:40,547 --> 00:38:41,632
The answer was no.

462
00:38:42,591 --> 00:38:44,467
I'm sure it's the same for you.

463
00:38:44,468 --> 00:38:45,885
We're just two individuals

464
00:38:45,886 --> 00:38:48,931
who lived different lives
for 30 years before crossing paths.

465
00:38:49,723 --> 00:38:51,642
If we click, that's great.

466
00:38:52,392 --> 00:38:55,354
But if we don't, there's no need
to stress or panic over it.

467
00:38:56,271 --> 00:38:58,564
- Well, I suppose so.
- Right.

468
00:38:58,565 --> 00:39:00,859
We're not that important
to each other.

469
00:39:02,778 --> 00:39:04,363
There's no point
in fighting like this.

470
00:39:07,532 --> 00:39:09,493
Let me ask you straight up.

471
00:39:12,412 --> 00:39:13,747
Up until now

472
00:39:15,040 --> 00:39:16,458
what was your actual deal with me?

473
00:39:22,047 --> 00:39:23,840
- Let's drink another glass.
- Sure.

474
00:39:39,564 --> 00:39:42,693
Do you honestly see yourself
as the victim here?

475
00:39:46,154 --> 00:39:49,365
What do you take
your team members for?

476
00:39:49,366 --> 00:39:50,367
I mean...

477
00:39:50,701 --> 00:39:53,870
Have you ever once consulted us

478
00:39:54,579 --> 00:39:56,873
before making critical decisions?

479
00:39:58,375 --> 00:40:03,254
I've never once felt like
a valued member of this team

480
00:40:03,255 --> 00:40:06,800
working alongside you
during my time here.

481
00:40:08,760 --> 00:40:10,053
Think about it.

482
00:40:10,721 --> 00:40:13,724
I didn't start out
treating you awfully.

483
00:40:19,396 --> 00:40:22,315
When I started working under you,
I promised myself.

484
00:40:22,733 --> 00:40:24,693
I'd stop expecting respect
just because I'm your senior.

485
00:40:24,943 --> 00:40:27,070
I'd just focus on doing my best
as a team member.

486
00:40:28,280 --> 00:40:29,781
But you?

487
00:40:31,450 --> 00:40:33,744
You have no respect for your team,
let alone senior respect.

488
00:40:35,037 --> 00:40:37,455
You never care
about what's going on in our heads

489
00:40:37,456 --> 00:40:39,331
or what struggles we face on the job.

490
00:40:39,332 --> 00:40:41,168
You never show an ounce of curiosity.

491
00:40:41,418 --> 00:40:45,255
All you care about is whether
something meets your standards.

492
00:40:46,298 --> 00:40:47,591
This is a workplace.

493
00:40:48,383 --> 00:40:50,009
We're here to get a job done.

494
00:40:50,010 --> 00:40:51,011
Right.

495
00:40:51,386 --> 00:40:52,929
That's your perspective.

496
00:40:55,974 --> 00:40:57,684
You may not feel the same way

497
00:40:58,393 --> 00:41:01,188
but to me,
you are an important person.

498
00:41:07,360 --> 00:41:08,903
As you know

499
00:41:08,904 --> 00:41:11,114
my batch didn't enter
through open recruitment.

500
00:41:11,573 --> 00:41:14,034
So our seniority
wasn't properly credited.

501
00:41:15,911 --> 00:41:17,369
But do you really think

502
00:41:17,370 --> 00:41:19,915
that's the only reason
you got promoted ahead of me?

503
00:41:21,041 --> 00:41:22,667
Are you saying there's more to it?

504
00:41:23,210 --> 00:41:24,211
Of course.

505
00:41:24,795 --> 00:41:26,838
You're simply better than me.

506
00:41:28,465 --> 00:41:30,425
Seniority aside

507
00:41:30,801 --> 00:41:34,095
I would've been promoted first
if I'd been more capable.

508
00:41:34,096 --> 00:41:35,555
That's how corporate works.

509
00:41:39,142 --> 00:41:41,311
But part of me
wanted to mess with you.

510
00:41:42,270 --> 00:41:45,482
You're younger than me,
but you seemed better than me.

511
00:41:48,693 --> 00:41:50,946
Now that I've said it out loud,
I sound like a total idiot.

512
00:41:57,035 --> 00:41:58,245
Don't say that.

513
00:41:59,913 --> 00:42:02,290
I thought I fully understood
your frustrations

514
00:42:03,291 --> 00:42:04,376
but I clearly didn't.

515
00:42:04,876 --> 00:42:05,877
I'm sorry.

516
00:42:07,170 --> 00:42:08,672
Anyway, I'm sorry.

517
00:42:09,756 --> 00:42:12,634
At the end of the day,
this happened because I fell short.

518
00:42:13,552 --> 00:42:16,429
Not at all. Hearing your side,
I wasn't entirely blameless.

519
00:42:19,516 --> 00:42:21,643
I'll hand in my resignation tomorrow.

520
00:42:22,519 --> 00:42:25,813
I'll handle all the handovers
before I leave

521
00:42:25,814 --> 00:42:26,815
so don't worry.

522
00:42:27,399 --> 00:42:28,482
Oh, right.

523
00:42:28,483 --> 00:42:29,775
When I acted friendly with Mr. Jeong

524
00:42:29,776 --> 00:42:32,821
I didn't mean to sweep
all the grudges under the rug.

525
00:42:33,113 --> 00:42:34,698
I meant to clear the air and move on.

526
00:42:39,077 --> 00:42:41,037
Is that really necessary?

527
00:42:44,082 --> 00:42:46,001
I don't have the stomach
to keep working here.

528
00:42:46,960 --> 00:42:49,254
I acted like a jerk
to my younger boss

529
00:42:50,505 --> 00:42:52,048
and got chewed out for it.

530
00:42:53,216 --> 00:42:54,884
By that logic,
I'm a lousy team leader

531
00:42:54,885 --> 00:42:57,011
who couldn't manage
a single team member

532
00:42:57,012 --> 00:42:59,431
and publicly humiliated him.

533
00:43:02,559 --> 00:43:03,560
To be honest

534
00:43:04,603 --> 00:43:06,437
I was thinking of quitting too.

535
00:43:06,438 --> 00:43:07,564
Truly.

536
00:43:09,357 --> 00:43:12,360
But if we both walk out now

537
00:43:13,945 --> 00:43:16,323
won't we just be quitting
because we lost to each other?

538
00:43:16,948 --> 00:43:18,491
Let's not do that.

539
00:43:21,077 --> 00:43:22,078
Mr. Yang.

540
00:43:23,413 --> 00:43:24,456
Well...

541
00:43:25,373 --> 00:43:27,792
Putting aside our personal clashes

542
00:43:28,627 --> 00:43:31,004
how do you
evaluate me professionally?

543
00:43:34,591 --> 00:43:35,717
I had those moments.

544
00:43:36,426 --> 00:43:39,137
Like, "I hate this guy's guts,
but he's good at his job."

545
00:43:40,347 --> 00:43:43,183
All the brands we brought in
were on the verge of tanking.

546
00:43:43,850 --> 00:43:45,143
I give you that.

547
00:43:46,102 --> 00:43:47,519
Your ability to see the big picture

548
00:43:47,520 --> 00:43:49,064
and push projects through
was impressive.

549
00:43:50,857 --> 00:43:51,900
I felt the same way.

550
00:43:52,984 --> 00:43:55,528
Even when I thought
we didn't click at all

551
00:43:56,238 --> 00:43:57,697
I couldn't deny your competence.

552
00:43:58,281 --> 00:44:00,116
I thought your years of experience
really showed.

553
00:44:00,867 --> 00:44:03,912
You've got an eye for details
that others overlook.

554
00:44:08,291 --> 00:44:09,292
You think so?

555
00:44:17,968 --> 00:44:19,469
Which brings me to my point.

556
00:44:21,513 --> 00:44:22,722
Let's team up.

557
00:44:24,307 --> 00:44:25,350
Team up?

558
00:44:25,642 --> 00:44:26,643
Mr. Yang.

559
00:44:28,144 --> 00:44:29,854
Do you want to shake things up
with me?

560
00:44:32,816 --> 00:44:34,985
You're making me feel uneasy.

561
00:44:38,405 --> 00:44:40,323
I'm going to turn
this company around.

562
00:44:43,201 --> 00:44:48,123
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

563
00:45:01,261 --> 00:45:03,847
GANGNAM

564
00:45:05,098 --> 00:45:07,266
Yes, sir, so...

565
00:45:07,267 --> 00:45:10,352
Take this chance to register
as a rental property business

566
00:45:10,353 --> 00:45:13,064
and learn how to issue
electronic tax invoices.

567
00:45:13,523 --> 00:45:15,149
That's how people trip
into tax evasion

568
00:45:15,150 --> 00:45:16,776
while trying to save on taxes.

569
00:45:17,694 --> 00:45:19,611
Yes, right.

570
00:45:19,612 --> 00:45:20,989
Okay, goodbye.

571
00:45:22,490 --> 00:45:24,159
Goodness, I'm sorry.

572
00:45:24,492 --> 00:45:25,868
- The call went on a bit too long.
- No.

573
00:45:25,869 --> 00:45:27,786
- It's fine.
- So you're looking

574
00:45:27,787 --> 00:45:29,789
into both commercial spaces
and apartments?

575
00:45:30,540 --> 00:45:33,042
Nothing's set in stone yet

576
00:45:33,043 --> 00:45:36,046
but my priority is
stable monthly rental income.

577
00:45:36,713 --> 00:45:38,088
Do you have enough capital?

578
00:45:38,089 --> 00:45:39,132
Or will you need a loan?

579
00:45:39,924 --> 00:45:41,717
I've budgeted for some

580
00:45:41,718 --> 00:45:44,345
but I'd rather avoid loans
if possible.

581
00:45:44,346 --> 00:45:47,598
You must be quite well-off
for someone young.

582
00:45:47,599 --> 00:45:49,516
- Are you an office worker?
- Yes.

583
00:45:49,517 --> 00:45:51,393
Smart choice.

584
00:45:51,394 --> 00:45:55,439
In this day and age, relying solely
on a salary gets you nowhere.

585
00:45:55,440 --> 00:45:56,523
If you have spare cash

586
00:45:56,524 --> 00:45:58,985
you need a solid fallback,
like owning a building.

587
00:46:00,862 --> 00:46:04,366
If I may ask,
what is your annual salary?

588
00:46:04,991 --> 00:46:06,910
Around 70 million won.

589
00:46:07,410 --> 00:46:08,952
Does that matter?

590
00:46:08,953 --> 00:46:11,246
Of course, it matters.

591
00:46:11,247 --> 00:46:14,417
That means your personal market value
is over three billion won.

592
00:46:14,793 --> 00:46:16,877
To take in 70 million a year in rent

593
00:46:16,878 --> 00:46:19,505
after taxes and expenses

594
00:46:19,506 --> 00:46:21,591
your property needs to be worth
at least three billion.

595
00:46:22,092 --> 00:46:24,259
Making that much in salary means

596
00:46:24,260 --> 00:46:27,012
you're walking around
with a three-billion-won price tag.

597
00:46:27,013 --> 00:46:28,306
We've got a VIP here.

598
00:46:30,392 --> 00:46:31,393
You're right.

599
00:46:31,768 --> 00:46:33,103
Hearing it that way

600
00:46:34,312 --> 00:46:36,021
I'm worth three billion.

601
00:46:36,022 --> 00:46:37,941
A lot of people buy lottery tickets
these days, right?

602
00:46:39,067 --> 00:46:42,487
That's because they don't realize
their own worth.

603
00:46:43,363 --> 00:46:45,949
Now, let's see.

604
00:46:46,491 --> 00:46:49,034
Apartments around this neighborhood
are solid.

605
00:46:49,035 --> 00:46:50,661
Commercial buildings
come with too many...

606
00:46:50,662 --> 00:46:51,745
Sir.

607
00:46:51,746 --> 00:46:54,207
I'm sorry,
but I'll come back another time.

608
00:46:54,457 --> 00:46:55,541
I'm sorry?

609
00:46:55,542 --> 00:46:56,875
Like you said

610
00:46:56,876 --> 00:46:59,754
a 3-billion-won guy shouldn't get
pushed around by 1.3 billion.

611
00:47:00,547 --> 00:47:01,965
What's this 1.3 billion won?

612
00:49:35,159 --> 00:49:37,161
Subtitles by Eunjin Erica Kim
